{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception interface, separating motion commands from sensor events. The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and conservative turn recovery is used for obstacles. Only in deadlock (blocked on all sides) is full_rotate used. All obstacle events force a recovery turn before returning to exploration. The design avoids oscillations and infinite controllable loops.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model robot's motion and perception as a single plant automaton with all controllable and uncontrollable events.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, coverage-biased exploration: random_walk in clear, move_forward for short progress, turn recovery for obstacles, and full_rotate only as last resort."
